      "font_size": 11.9,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 666,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p21_b6",
      "text": "Choice of ambiguity geometry.\nThe choice of the \u21131 ambiguity set is equally practical.\nThe promptwise adversary has a dual-norm form for general \u2113p geometry, but \u21131 is the\ncase that turns this structure into a water-filling policy and a sampled RLHF bonus.\nIn the algorithm, its key advantage is locality: the robust correction can be written in\nterms of the probability assigned to the threatening sampled response rather than the\nentire hidden simplex. The next proposition makes this statement precise by comparing\n\u2113p ambiguity geometries through the bonus factor attached to a vertex response.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        384.7,
        525.6,
        506.0
